R"VG(
# futuristic7.vg (H-04's second pass): the assembly's vote (the question, the debate, the reasons on both sides, the result: each a
# people's own: what they quarrel about is their feasts, their herds, their crafts, their colours) and the code of law (its sections
# composed, the people's values and faith in them).

# ---- the assembly's vote: its parts --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vt.question
  The question: whether to {vt.what}.
  Put to the assembly: whether to {vt.what}.
  The motion: to {vt.what}.
  The proposal, brought by {#n|family}: to {vt.what}.
vt.what (share=0.6)
  open the {fut.block} again, the empty ones
  let the machines choose the weather
  build a second {fut.green}
  close the transit line at night
  send a ship to {vt.where}
  give the archive a voice in the assembly
  keep {festival} for a whole cycle
  let the {herd} out of the pens and into the hills
  teach {craft} in the schools again
  paint the {fut.gate} {colour.any}
  move {festival} to {season.next}
  take down the old {fut.sys.n}
  let children vote at fifteen
  rename the {fut.common} after {founder}
  plant {tree} along {streets.of}
  forbid {pastime} in the {fut.common} after midnight
  ask the machines to stop greeting people by name
  keep a {beast} in the school
  allow fires of {fuel} in the courts at {festival}
  stop counting the cycles, and count something else
  make {drink} again, the old way
  let the {fut.green} go wild for a year
  build a model of {focusword} for the children
  open {holyplace} at night
  bring back {instrument} for the evening bells
  serve {food} at every assembly, to shorten the speeches
  hang {colour.holy} lamps along {streets.of}
  keep the old word {~home} on the signs
  (has:$home.landmark) clear the ground round {$home.landmark}
  (contact=1 othergone=0) send envoys to the {other}
  (stage>=1) leave {$home} for {city}
  (stage>=1 inv.sleep=1) join the sleepers
  (stage>=1) close the {fut.block}
  (stage>=1) send the children to {city2}
vt.where
  (moons>0) {moon}
  the dark rocks
  (giant=1) the wanderer
  the other worlds of {sun.first}
  (rings=1) the ring
  (companion=1) the second sun
  the far side of {sun.first}

vt.debate (share=0.7)
  {#n} spoke. The longest speech was about {vt.topic}.
  The debate began {fut.when.past} and went on long after, and most of it was about {vt.topic}.
  {vt.someone} spoke for an hour about {vt.topic}, and changed nobody's mind.
  There was shouting, briefly, about {vt.topic}. Then {food} was brought in.
  Nobody spoke for a long time. Then everyone did.
  The {craft} workshop spoke as one, which has never happened before.
  Someone brought the {herd} into the hall to make a point. The point was made.
  It was argued in the old way, standing, with {drink} for the speakers.
vt.topic
  the {herd}
  what {founder} would have wanted
  the cost
  the children
  the last time this was asked
  {festival}
  the colour of the {fut.gate}
  the old records
  the {fut.green}
vt.someone
  The oldest resident
  Someone from the {craft} workshop
  One of the young ones
  A woman from the {fut.block}
  A man who keeps the {herd}
  The keeper of the archive

vt.for
  For: {vt.reason}. {=.short}
  Those for it said that {vt.reason}.
  {vt.someone} spoke for it: {vt.reason}.
vt.against
  (.short=1) Against: {vt.reason2}.
  (!has:.short) Those against it said that {vt.reason2}.
  (!has:.short) The other side: {vt.reason2}.
vt.reason
  (1) {vt.reason.plain}
  {vt.reason.own}
  {vt.reason.own}
  {vt.reason.own}
vt.reason.plain (share=0.3)
  we have the time and the means
  our grandparents would have done it
  the young want it
  nothing else is working
  it would be beautiful
  it costs nothing but effort
vt.reason.own (share=0.85)
  it is what {founder} would have done, with the {herd} and the {crop} as they were
  the children asked, at {feast.custom}, and nobody could say why not
  it has been done at {city2}, and their {fut.green} are still standing
  it would make {festival} better, and {food} easier to come by
  it is a matter of {virtue}
  we promised it at the last vote, over {drink}
  the {herd} would like it
  the old saying is right: {proverb}
  the {craft} workshop has offered to do it for nothing
  the {herd} have done without it long enough
  {festival} was better when we did it, with {instrument}
  it would put {colour.holy} back on the {fut.gate}
vt.reason2
  (1) {vt.reason2.plain}
  {vt.reason2.own}
  {vt.reason2.own}
  {vt.reason2.own}

vt.reason2.plain (share=0.3)
  we do not need it
  it was tried before
  the machines are against it
  it would change nothing
  it is too soon
  nobody would look after it
vt.reason2.own (share=0.85)
  it would upset the {herd}
  it is {vice}, dressed up as {virtue}
  the old ones in the {fut.block} would hate it
  it would cost us {festival}, or the {food} at it
  it is what {city2} did, and look at their {fut.green}
  the water will not stretch to it, not with the {crop} to think of
  {proverb}, and that settles it
  the {herd} would not stand for it
  the {craft} workshop would have to stop for a season
  it would mean less {food} at {festival}
  the old ones swore {oath} against it once, and an oath is an oath
  the {bird} nest there, and always have
vt.result
  (1) {vt.result.plain}
  (2) {vt.result.own}
vt.result.own (share=0.8)
  Carried, and {instrument} was played in the {fut.common} until late.
  Lost. The {craft} workshop has promised to bring it back next {festival}.
  Carried; the {herd} were the first to be told, by tradition.
  Tied. Settled the old way, by {fut.game}; the motion won.
  Carried, and the {colour.holy} lamps lit over the {fut.gate} to say so.
  Lost, and {food} was served anyway, as the custom is.
  Carried after a recount, done by hand, by the children, twice.
vt.result.plain (share=0.5)
  The vote: for, by {#nbig}. It will be done.
  The vote: against, by {#nbig}. It will not be done, this cycle.
  The vote was tied. It will be asked again at {festival}.
  The vote: for, by one. Nobody is happy.
  Carried, with {#n} abstaining, all of them asleep.
  Lost. Its friends have gone to the {fut.common} to sulk.
  Carried. Work begins in {season.next}.
  Withdrawn before the vote, to everyone's relief.
  Carried by acclamation; nobody counted.
  Lost by {#n}. It will come back; it always does.
  Deferred until the {herd} are in.
  Carried; the machines have been told, and have no objection.
  Lost, and the hall emptied in silence.
  Carried, and {instrument} was played in the {fut.common} until late.

# ---- the code of law ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.law (words=36..140)
  {law.head}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.end}
  {law.head}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.end}
  {law.head}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.art}\n{law.end}

law.head (formula people=3)
  The code of {$seat}, as revised in cycle {#year:digits}. Part {n}.
  Laws of {$seat}, the section on {law.topic}.
  From the laws of {$seat}, as the assembly last agreed them.
  The law of {$home}, {law.topic}, as read at {festival}.
law.topic
  the gardens
  the machines
  the archive
  leaving and returning
  the water
  the children
  the herds
  the dead
  the feasts

law.art
  (3 once) Section {n}: {law.who} {law.may} {law.what}{law.unless}.
  (3 once) Section {n}: {law.who} {law.may} {law.what}{law.unless}.
  (2 once) Section {n}: {law.who} {law.may} {law.what}{law.unless}.
  (2 once) Section {n}: {law.custom}
  (1 once) Section {n}: {law.custom}
  (1 once) Section {n}: {law.value}
law.who (people=8)
  no person
  every person
  a child
  a machine
  the assembly
  a stranger
  the keepers of the archive
  anyone who leaves the habitat
  the keepers of the {herd}
  a person in mourning
  the watch at the {fut.gate}
  a guest at {festival}
law.may
  may
  may not
  must
  must not
  may at any time
law.what (share=0.7)
  be held without the assembly's leave
  alter the archive, only add to it
  close the {fut.green} while any person is hungry
  harm a person, or allow harm it could stop
  refuse the machines' teaching, and be taught by a person instead
  enter a home without being asked
  take more water than the season allows
  leave in the dark season without telling the watch
  decide for a person what the person can decide
  speak at the assembly, once each season
  paint over {motif.over} on another's door
  keep a {beast} in the {fut.green}
  light fires of {fuel} inside the walls
  sell {food} at {festival}
  wear {colour.mourn} except for the dead
  play {fut.game} for anything but small stakes
  take one of the {herd} from the pens without the keeper
  turn away a stranger at the {fut.gate}
law.unless
  (2)
  , unless the assembly agrees
  , except in danger to life
  , for any reason
  , and the reason is to be recorded
  , except at {festival}
  , unless the {herd} need it
law.custom (share=0.7)
  the names of the dead are kept, and read at {festival}.
  no record may be destroyed, even by the one it is about.
  {festival} is kept by all; no work is asked of anyone that day.
  the {herd} in the pens belong to all, and their keepers are owed {food} and thanks.
  every child is taught {craft} until they can do it, or until they can say why not.
  the old word {~law} is kept at the head of this code, though nobody can say it well.
  a dispute about the {fut.green} is settled in the {fut.green}, standing up.
  the dead are carried to {deadplace} by their neighbours, not by machines.
law.value
  (value=trade) every exchange is recorded, and every record is public.
  (value=learning) every person may read every record, except their neighbours' letters.
  (value=art) no wall may stay bare for more than a cycle.
  (value=war) every adult keeps a weapon, and none may carry it into {town.open}.
  (value=piety) {holyplace} is open to all, at all hours.
  (faith=machine) no person may be asked to obey a machine they do not understand.
  (faith!=machine) the machines may advise on the {fut.green} and on everything else; they may not decide.

law.end (formula)
  So agreed.
  Recorded at {$seat}.
  Revised at the {#number:ord} reading; to be read again in ten cycles.
  Agreed, after {#n} sittings. Recorded by the archive.
)VG"
